{
  "feature_instruction": "This feature implements the complete online ordering flow for Hotel Chul Mutton Baner, allowing users to add menu items to a cart, proceed to checkout, provide delivery details, and view their order history. It integrates with the `menu-display` feature to fetch menu items and the `order-management-api` feature to create and retrieve orders.\n\n## Design Tokens\n- Navbar: bg-[#A0522D] text-white\n- Primary CTA: bg-[#FF4500] hover:bg-[#E04000] text-white font-semibold rounded-full px-8 py-3 transition-all duration-200\n- Brand text accent: text-[#A0522D]\n- Section bg: bg-[#FFF8E1] (odd sections) / bg-[#FDF5E6] (even sections)\n- Card: bg-white rounded-xl shadow-md border border-gray-100 p-6\n- Section container: <section className=\"py-16 px-4\"><div className=\"max-w-7xl mx-auto\">\n- Hero h1: text-4xl md:text-6xl font-bold text-white\n- Body: text-[#362419] leading-relaxed\n\n### `frontend/src/types/local/cart.ts`\nThis file defines the TypeScript types for the local shopping cart, including `CartItem` and `Cart` interfaces. `CartItem` represents a single item in the cart, containing `menuItemId` (UUID), `name` (string), `price` (number), `quantity` (number), and `imageUrl` (string). `Cart` contains an array of `CartItem`s and a `totalAmount` (number).\n\n### `frontend/src/services/local/cartService.ts`\nThis service provides functions to interact with the browser's `localStorage` for persisting and retrieving the cart state. It exports `getCart(): Cart`, `saveCart(cart: Cart): void`, `addItemToCart(item: CartItem): Cart`, `removeItemFromCart(menuItemId: UUID): Cart`, `updateItemQuantity(menuItemId: UUID, quantity: number): Cart`, and `clearCart(): void`. These functions ensure the cart data is always synchronized with `localStorage`.\n\n### `frontend/src/context/CartContext.tsx`\nThis React context manages the global state of the user's shopping cart. It provides `cart` (Cart), `addItem` (function), `removeItem` (function), `updateQuantity` (function), and `clearCart` (function) to its consumers. It uses `cartService.ts` to persist and load the cart from `localStorage`. The `CartProvider` component wraps the application or relevant parts, making the cart state available to all nested components.\n\n### `frontend/src/types/order.ts`\nThis file defines the TypeScript types for orders and order items, mirroring the backend `order-management-api` contracts. It includes `OrderItemRequest` (menuItemId: UUID, quantity: number), `CreateOrderRequest` (orderItems: OrderItemRequest[], deliveryAddress: string, orderType: 'DELIVERY' | 'PICKUP'), `OrderItemResponse` (orderItemId: UUID, menuItem: MenuItemDto, quantity: number, subtotal: number), and `OrderResponse` (orderId: UUID, userId: number, orderType: 'DELIVERY' | 'PICKUP', orderStatus: 'PENDING' | 'CONFIRMED' | 'PREPARING' | 'READY_FOR_PICKUP' | 'OUT_FOR_DELIVERY' | 'DELIVERED' | 'CANCELLED', totalAmount: number, orderDate: string, deliveryAddress: string, orderItems: OrderItemResponse[]).\n\n### `frontend/src/services/orderService.ts`\nThis service handles API calls related to orders. It exports `createOrder(order: CreateOrderRequest): Promise<OrderResponse>` which makes a POST request to `/api/v1/orders`, `getOrderById(orderId: UUID): Promise<OrderResponse>` which makes a GET request to `/api/v1/orders/{orderId}`, and `getMyOrders(): Promise<OrderResponse[]>` which makes a GET request to `/api/v1/orders/my-orders`. It uses the `api/client.ts` for making authenticated HTTP requests.\n\n### `frontend/src/hooks/useOrders.ts`\nThis custom React hook provides an interface for components to interact with order data. It exposes `createOrder` (async function), `getOrderById` (async function), `myOrders` (OrderResponse[]), `loading` (boolean), `error` (Error | null), and `fetchMyOrders` (async function). It utilizes `orderService.ts` to perform the actual API calls and manages the loading and error states.\n\n### `frontend/src/components/order/CartSummary.tsx`\nThis component displays a summary of the items currently in the cart. It consumes the `CartContext` to get the `cart` state. It shows each `CartItem` with its name, quantity, price, and subtotal, along with the total amount of the entire cart. It includes buttons to adjust item quantities or remove items from the cart, which trigger `updateQuantity` and `removeItem` from `CartContext`.\n\n### `frontend/src/components/order/DeliveryAddressForm.tsx`\nThis component provides a form for users to enter their delivery address and contact information. It should capture fields like `fullName`, `phoneNumber`, `streetAddress`, `city`, `state`, and `zipCode`. It includes validation for these fields and an `onSubmit` prop that receives the validated address data. The form should be styled with Tailwind CSS, reflecting the earthy and premium design tokens.\n\n### `frontend/src/components/order/PaymentOptions.tsx`\nThis component allows users to select a payment method. For the initial implementation, it will simulate a successful payment. It should present options like \"Cash on Delivery\" or \"Pay Online (Simulated)\". Upon selection and confirmation, it will trigger an `onPaymentSuccess` callback, which will be handled by `CheckoutPage.tsx`.\n\n### `frontend/src/pages/CheckoutPage.tsx`\nThis page orchestrates the multi-step checkout process. It uses `CartContext` to access cart data and `useOrders` to create a new order. The page will have distinct sections for \"Cart Summary\", \"Delivery Information\", and \"Payment\".\n\n**Sections:**\n1.  **Cart Summary:** Displays the `CartSummary` component, allowing users to review and make final adjustments to their order before proceeding. Heading: <h2 className=\"text-3xl font-bold text-[#A0522D] mb-6\">Your Order Summary</h2>\n2.  **Delivery Information:** Displays the `DeliveryAddressForm` component. Once the address is submitted, the page transitions to the payment step. Heading: <h2 className=\"text-3xl font-bold text-[#A0522D] mb-6\">Where should we deliver?</h2>\n3.  **Payment:** Displays the `PaymentOptions` component. Upon successful payment (simulated), the page calls `useOrders().createOrder()` with the collected cart items and delivery address. After the order is successfully created, the user is redirected to the `OrderConfirmationPage` with the `orderId`.\n\nThe page should handle loading and error states from `useOrders`. The overall layout uses `<Layout>` from `core-ui`.\n\n### `frontend/src/pages/OrderConfirmationPage.tsx`\nThis page displays a summary of a successfully placed order. It receives the `orderId` as a URL parameter. It uses `useOrders().getOrderById(orderId)` to fetch the complete order details. If the order is found, it displays the order ID, total amount, delivery address, estimated delivery time (placeholder), and a list of ordered items. It includes a call to action to \"Continue Shopping\" (linking to `/menu`) or \"View My Orders\" (linking to `/my-orders`). The page should handle loading and error states. The overall layout uses `<Layout>` from `core-ui`.\n\n**Sections:**\n1.  **Confirmation Message:** <h1 className=\"text-4xl md:text-5xl font-bold text-[#A0522D] mb-4\">Order Confirmed!</h1> <p className=\"text-xl text-[#362419] mb-8\">Thank you for choosing Hotel Chul Mutton Baner. Your culinary journey is about to begin!</p>\n2.  **Order Details:** Displays the fetched `OrderResponse` details. Each item in the order should show its name, quantity, and subtotal. Heading: <h2 className=\"text-3xl font-bold text-[#A0522D] mb-6\">Your Order Details</h2>\n3.  **Call to Action:** Buttons for \"Continue Shopping\" and \"View My Orders\".\n\n### `frontend/src/pages/OrderHistoryPage.tsx`\nThis page allows logged-in users to view their past orders. It uses `useOrders().fetchMyOrders()` to retrieve a list of all orders placed by the current user. It displays each order in a card or table format, showing the `orderId`, `orderDate`, `totalAmount`, `orderStatus`, and a button to view `OrderResponse` details (linking to `/order-confirmation/{orderId}`). The page should handle loading and error states. If no orders are found, it displays a message like \"You haven't placed any orders yet.\" The overall layout uses `<Layout>` from `core-ui`.\n\n**Sections:**\n1.  **Page Title:** <h1 className=\"text-4xl md:text-5xl font-bold text-[#A0522D] mb-8\">My Order History</h1>\n2.  **Order List:** Displays a list of `OrderResponse` objects. Each order should be presented clearly with key details and a link to its confirmation page.\n",
